#: Game.Levels.DemoWorld.L06
msgid "Now, you can perform `induction m`. This will induct over the whole statement of `∀ (n : Nat), m = n ∨ m ≠ n`, which then can be attacked with case analysis."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.PrimeImpliesIrreducible.LV01_CancellationInNat
msgid "In this level, we prove the cancellation law for natural numbers.\n"
"That is, if multiplying two numbers by a non zero natural number gives the same result,\n"
"then the original numbers must be equal."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.DemoWorld.L03
msgid "Now, try to use the fact that `pred (k+1) = k` for any `k` and compose this with your hypothesis `«{h}»` and `congrArg`."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.DemoWorld.L05
msgid "You might again try the trick of making `goal` become `False` and then rewriting your assumptions such that they are trivially contradictory."
msgstr ""

